Multi-outlet food ordering with stock concurrency - Also, we can use same for blinkit

The strongest way to attempt this problem is to design around one rule:
Never sell stock you don't have, and never hold a lock while doing slow work like payment.

1. Stock is per ingredient.
2. View menu of outlet, show items only in stock
3. Place multi-item order from one outlet
4. Reverse stock, pay and then confirm, if payment fails return reversed stock back
5. No overselling, when multiple concurrent order in place
6. Idempotent order placement, so a double click don't place 2 orders

Entities -

Stock: Class
String id, Ingredient ingredient, int quantity

Ingredient: Class
String id, String name

MenuItem: Class
String id, List<Item> items

Outlet: Class
String id, String name, MenuItem menu, Stock stock

Item: Class
String id, String name, Map<Ingredient, quantity> recipe, double price

Order: Class
String orderId, String orderPlaceBy, OrderItem item, double totalAmount,
String outletId, OrderStatus orderStatus

OrderItem: Class
String orderItemId, Map<Item, Integer> itemQuantityDetails, boolean isAvailable

OrderStatus: Enum
CREATED, STOCK_REVERSED, CONFIRM, CANCELLED, FAILED

Services -

InventoryService: Class
- addItemInStock(Map<Ingredient, Integer> itemsToAddStock)
- getOutletMenu(String OutletId)
- reserveItemStock(List<Item> items, String orderId)
- releaseStock(String orderId)


OrderService: Class
- placeOrder(OrderItem orderItem, String orderPlacedBy, String outletId, String idempotencyKey)
- cancelOrder(String orderId)

PaymentService: Class
- processPayment(String orderId, double amount)
